cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "juliaTDGL: a three-dimensional two-band time-dependent Ginzburg-Landau solver"
message: >
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Robles Calderón
    given-names: Jorge Alfredo
    alias: georgeotjg
    affiliation: Universidad Nacional de Colombia
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-0557-0263"
abstract: >
  Three-dimensional two-band time-dependent Ginzburg-Landau solver in Julia for the
  geometric superconducting diode effect in two-gap superconductors (MgB2 as target).
  Link variables, self-consistent vector potential, optional scalar potential by Coulomb
  projection, Josephson voltmeter with a crossing-count verdict rule, and a production scheme
  with the curl-curl term implicit and the light band in substeps. Optional terms, all off
  by default, add interband drag, a temperature field with Joule heating, a diffused gauge
  residual and a bath temperature.
keywords:
  - time-dependent Ginzburg-Landau
  - superconducting diode effect
  - two-band superconductivity
  - MgB2
  - vortex dynamics
  - Julia
